Line comments: inside code, two semicolons comment out the rest of the line. In prose; a semicolon is just text.
$[Import* std]
${+ 1   ;; the first operand; } ] " $missing are ignored
    2}  ;; a semicolon after a region is ordinary prose
expect: 3
${++ "a;b" ";"}
expect: "a;b;"
${+ 1 ;{a raw body; with a semicolon} 2}
expect: 3
$[# twice {^ {x}
    ;; Doubles the input.
    ;; Used below.
    [# d {* 2 x}]   ;; a trailing comment after a form
    d}]
${twice 21}
expect: 42
${' 1;;no space needed after a token
}
expect: [1]
$[f "Sum: ${+ 1 ;; ignore } and ] here
    2}."]
expect: "Sum: 3."
$[f "Sum: ${+ 1 ;[ignore $missing and {}] 2}."]
expect: "Sum: 3."
